<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="CcpClient.Desktop.Features.Goon.GoonHostWindow"
        Title="Goon Game — Practice"
        Width="1280" Height="800"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterScreen"
        Background="#0b0b16">
  <!--
    Goon practice host shell (the landed IntakeHostWindow pattern). The embedded
    NativeWebView is the WINDOWS surface (WebView2). The Linux NativeWebDialog path is NOT
    ADMITTED: the goon page's bridge speaks window.chrome.webview only (goon/bridge.js:45-47,
    :65-67, :93-95), so a dialog would run the page STANDALONE — it would synthesize its own
    init (goon/bridge.js:473) and silently ignore every one of this host's door refusals. Where the
    embedded capability is not Available the honest surface shows: typed, never a substitute.

    THE REFUSAL RAIL on the right is not decoration and is not dismissible. Four of the title
    screen's items lead into goon-game-census.md §6 and the page's own refusals for all four
    are FALSE in this build (see GoonDoors). This rail is where the true sentence lives, and it
    is beside the page rather than behind a click for exactly that reason.
  -->
  <DockPanel>
    <TextBlock x:Name="Status" DockPanel.Dock="Bottom"
               Foreground="#ff9ad5" Background="#141422" Padding="6"
               FontFamily="Consolas" FontSize="12"
               Text="goon host booting" />

    <!--
      THE PROBE LINE. The layout-probe pattern (MainWindow.axaml.cs ProbeLine),
      applied to this window for the same reason it exists there: Avalonia gives Panel/Border no
      UIA peer, so the web host's rect is unreadable from outside, and the headed harness has to
      aim CopyFromScreen somewhere.

      It carries MORE than a rect, and that is the point. Every field is a state the harness must
      be able to REFUSE on before it reads a pixel: which surface was selected (a missing WebView2
      runtime lands in `surface`), whether the navigation succeeded, how many heartbeats the page
      has sent, and — read back out of the page's OWN object graph — whether init and manifest
      actually landed there. A capture that silently photographs a loader or an error page is the
      worst outcome this surface can produce, and this line is what makes it impossible.

      CONTENT-FREE by construction: an enum, two booleans, a count, a screen id, a display name
      that is a constant, and a rectangle. Never a file name, never a path, never the bridge token.
    -->
    <TextBlock x:Name="ProbeText" DockPanel.Dock="Bottom"
               AutomationProperties.AutomationId="GoonProbe"
               Foreground="#7a7a99" Background="#141422" Padding="6,2"
               FontFamily="Consolas" FontSize="11"
               Text="goon-probe: pending" />

    <Border x:Name="RefusalRail" DockPanel.Dock="Right"
            Width="340" Background="#141422" BorderBrush="#2a2a44" BorderThickness="1,0,0,0">
      <ScrollViewer>
        <StackPanel Margin="16" Spacing="12">
          <TextBlock Foreground="#ff9ad5" FontSize="16" FontWeight="Bold"
                     Text="This build plays Practice only" />
          <TextBlock x:Name="RailLead" Foreground="#c8c8dd" TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12"
                     Text="Practice is a complete duel against the scripted opponent. Four other menu items are not in this build, and the page's own explanations for them are wrong here — these are the real ones." />
          <StackPanel x:Name="RefusalPanel" Spacing="12" />
        </StackPanel>
      </ScrollViewer>
    </Border>

    <Panel>
      <StackPanel x:Name="UnsupportedPanel" IsVisible="False" Margin="24" Spacing="8">
        <TextBlock Foreground="#ff9ad5" FontSize="18" FontWeight="Bold"
                   Text="Goon Game: honest unsupported" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="UnsupportedDetail" Foreground="#c8c8dd" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
      </StackPanel>
      <!-- NativeWebView is created PROGRAMMATICALLY on the embedded path only (the spike L4
           lesson: in the tree it starts its adapter whenever the window shows). -->
      <Panel x:Name="WebHost" />
    </Panel>
  </DockPanel>
</Window>
